<title>POLAND: KPW clears Amerbank new issue for trade.</title>
<headline>KPW clears Amerbank new issue for trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade the new issue of Bank Amerykanski w Polsce SA (Amerbank), the KPW said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>No of Shares Offered: 1,500,000</p>
<p>Subscription Period:  May 5-12  Lead Manager:	   Amerbrokers</p>
<p> Price (PLN):	    N/A</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:     N/A</p>
<p>Use Of Proceeds: increasing the bank's own funds to expand</p>
<p>credit activity, expanding investment activity </p>
<p> EARNINGS DATA	   1996		   1995 (in million of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:	     9.03		   6.45</p>
<p> Interest Revenues:   52.04		  44.47</p>
<p>Main Shareholder:</p>
<p>Oil and gas firm  Polskie Gornictwo Naftowe i Gazownictwo -</p>
<p>24 pct of shareholder votes</p>
<p>No of Existing Shares: 4,200,000</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
